OL,4,CFamily prepare to eat 52-year-old      
OL,5,CChristmas pudding                      
OL,6,GA woman preparing to tuck into her     
OL,7,Glate grandmother's 52-year-old         
OL,8,GChristmas pudding with her family says 
OL,9,Gif they get E. coli from the           
OL,10,Gtraditional dessert "so be it".        
OL,12,FDaphne Townsend, who lived near        
OL,13,FTetbury, made her family the steamed   
OL,14,Fpudding in September 1974, something   
OL,15,Fshe did each year to give the festive  
OL,16,Ftreat three months to mature ahead of  
OL,17,Fthe big day.                           
OL,19,FShe died in 1975 but her family kept   
OL,20,Fthe pudding and have decided to make   
OL,21,FSunday the day they enjoy her culinary 
OL,22,Fskills one last time.             G2/4 
